diff --git a/guild-idler-status.md b/guild-idler-status.md
index df5947c..38da080 100644
--- a/guild-idler-status.md
+++ b/guild-idler-status.md
@@ -22643,3 +22643,22 @@ pre-redesign versions to confirm none were dropped, renamed, or
 rewired -- the request was explicit that nothing functional should be
 lost. No `SAVE_VERSION` bump needed -- markup, CSS, and local component
 state only, no `GameState` shape touched anywhere in this patch.
+
+
+### Chain first-clear success no longer free-rides on out-leveling; raids list sorted by unlock level (patch 0286)
+
+```discord-update
+Dev Update | Patch 0286
+- Fixed: a Story Quest chain's first playthrough was sitting at a flat ~95% success no matter the difficulty once a hero had out-leveled it -- odds now scale with your hero's current level and gear, same as an ordinary contract
+- Changed: the Raids list is now sorted by the level it unlocks at, instead of a mixed order
+```
+
+**Reported directly**: Story Quest chain stages (Sir Bramble, Lv 22) showing a flat 95% success across Easy and Normal difficulty alike, while ordinary board contracts for the same hero at the same gear spread realistically from 61% to 95% by difficulty. Screenshot evidence for both lists made the gap obvious at a glance.
+
+**Root cause: `QuestManager.chainOffer` never got the patch 0259 fix.** Patch 0259 ("Raid & Chain Replay success now re-baselines to current level") fixed the exact same bug for raids and for chain *replays* -- both were feeding a permanently fixed reqLevel into `previewSuccess`, whose `levelGapBonus = (hero.level - offer.reqLevel) * quest_reqlevel.levelGapSuccessCoefficient` term (and the parallel `autoGrowthSuccess - baselineSuccess` term) climbs without bound as a hero out-levels a fixed reqLevel -- confirmed at the time as "the one lever that can still reach MAX_SUCCESS on its own." `chainReplayOffer` was fixed by baking `reqLevel: Math.max(chain.reqLevel, heroLevel)` into the offer at generation. `RaidManager` got its own `successBaselineLevel` helper doing the same thing. Neither fix touched `chainOffer` -- the offer generated for a chain stage's *first* clear, which is what the shared chain board (`generateChainBoard`) and Auto-Chain's `tryContinueAutoChain` both actually use. That function still stores the chain's original fixed `chain.reqLevel` (whatever it was when the chain was first authored/discovered, often single digits for an early chain) straight into the offer, and nothing ever re-baselined it before this patch. Confirmed against `quest-chains.json`: exactly the stages shown in the report have low fixed reqLevels well below the hero's actual level.
+
+**Fixed in `previewSuccess` itself, not in `chainOffer`.** Rather than mutate `offer.reqLevel` the way the raid/replay fix did, this patch adds a local `successReqLevel = offer.chain ? Math.max(offer.reqLevel, hero.level) : offer.reqLevel` right inside `previewSuccess`, and uses that (instead of `offer.reqLevel`) for both the `baselineStats` split and `levelGapBonus`. Deliberately scoped this way because `offer.reqLevel` itself is read by three other things that must NOT change: `DiscoveredQuestsPanel`'s own `hero.level >= offer.reqLevel` eligibility filter (mutating reqLevel upward would gate lower-level heroes out of a chain stage they should still be able to see), the loot itemLevel roll in `resolve()`, and `chainOffer`'s own reward-gold/xp formulas (both explicitly keyed to `chain.reqLevel` directly per patch 0217's own confirmed scope). Re-baselining only inside `previewSuccess` fixes success and nothing else, and since `previewSuccess` is called fresh on every render (not just at commit), this also fixes the live board preview, not only the locked-in roll at `QuestManager.start`. Applies uniformly to every `offer.chain` (first-clear and replay both) rather than branching on `offer.chain.replay` -- for a replay, `offer.reqLevel` is already at-or-above `hero.level` by construction, so `Math.max` there is a no-op; for a first-clear stage, it's the actual fix. Never lowers success below what the chain's own authored reqLevel would give an at-or-under-level hero -- only removes the free ride past it.
+
+**Raids list ordering**, unrelated bug found in the same screenshot set: `RaidsPanel`'s raid list renders `RAIDS` straight from `raids.json`'s own array order, which was never level-ordered (`requiem_last_god`, reqLevel 55, sat at index 2, ahead of four lower-level raids). `LorePanel`'s own "completed raids" list already explicitly re-sorts by `reqLevel` (`RAIDS.filter(...).sort((a, b) => a.reqLevel - b.reqLevel)`), confirming reqLevel is already the intended canonical order elsewhere in the codebase -- `RaidsPanel` was just never updated to match. Fixed by reordering `raids.json` itself (ascending `reqLevel`) rather than sorting at render time, so every consumer of `RAIDS` gets the same order for free without a scattered `.sort()` at each call site. Checked for any behavior that depends on array position before reordering: `isRaidUnlocked` treats `RAIDS.findIndex(...) === 0` as "always unlocked" (the guild's starter raid) -- `blackford_keep` (reqLevel 8) was already the lowest-level raid in the set, so it lands at index 0 again after the sort and this special case is unaffected. Every other unlock gate (`unlocksRaidId`, `requiresChainId`) is looked up by id, not index, so reordering the array has zero effect on any raid's actual unlock logic -- confirmed by reading `RAID_BY_ID`/`isRaidUnlocked`/`raidLockReason` and the full `unlocksRaidId` graph (`blackford_keep` -> `frozen_wyrmkeep` -> `bonewrought_vault`, everything else ungated by a prior raid) before making the change.
+
+**Verified:** `npx tsc --noEmit` and `npx vite build --config vite.web.config.ts` both pass clean. No `SAVE_VERSION` bump needed -- no `GameState` shape changed; `chainOffer`'s stored `reqLevel` and `rewardGold`/`rewardXp` are byte-identical to before, only the runtime `previewSuccess` calculation and the static `raids.json` array order changed. Worth a real playtest confirming an out-leveled hero's chain-stage odds now track their board-contract odds at the same difficulty, and that the Raids tab now lists Blackford Keep through Requiem for the Last God in ascending level order.
